The legal texts come from the Presidency of the Republic of Brazil (Casa Civil), Planalto legislation portal:

  Texto oficial: Presidência da República, Casa Civil, https://www.planalto.gov.br/ccivil_03/,
  read through Internet Archive copies of the Planalto pages (capture timestamps in tools/sources.json),
  retrieved 28 October 2026. Este texto não substitui o publicado no Diário Oficial da União.

Official acts, laws and judicial decisions are not protected by copyright in Brazil (Lei 9.610/1998, art. 8º, IV).

Changes made by Lexifina: the annotated text was converted to one Markdown file per article, one paragraph per line;
spacing, quotes, dashes and label typesetting were normalised; Planalto's amendment notes were removed from the text
and used only to date and credit each change; and the versions were arranged as git commits credited to the
amendments that made each change. The wording of the law was not changed. The Presidency does not endorse this
repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
